<title>USA: U.S. CFTC backs easing in exchange rule reviews.</title>
<headline>U.S. CFTC backs easing in exchange rule reviews.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Futures Trading Commission voted Thursday to revise its procedures for reviewing and approving applications for new futures exchange contracts.</p>
<p>The agency also approved new procedures for reviewing exchange rules. The changes are part of an ongoing effort by the CFTC to streamline regulations to reduce regulatory burdens and delays.</p>
<p>In other action, the agency approved the Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa Exchange's application to trade futures and options on Basic Formula Price Milk.</p>
</text>
